# Declarative map of every credential the protected release lanes need.
#
# FORMAT (whitespace separated, four columns):
#   <github-environment>  <secret-name>  <source>  <required|optional>
#
# A source is either an `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>` 1Password reference, or a
# `derive:` rule the script computes. Item titles use an EN DASH, matching
# 1Password exactly; a hyphen will not resolve.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A CREDENTIAL. It names where credentials come from,
# not what they are. It is committed deliberately so the credential surface of
# this repository is reviewable in the tree.

# The Backblaze endpoint and region are DERIVED, not stored. They are not
# independent facts -- they are determined by the account the application key
# belongs to, and b2_authorize_account states them. Storing a transcribed copy
# would just be a second place for them to be wrong.
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ENDPOINT    derive:b2-s3-endpoint                                          required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_REGION      derive:b2-s3-region                                            required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ACCESS_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/keyID               required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_SECRET_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/applicationKey      required

recovery-live       HCLOUD_TOKEN                        op://Personal/Keepling – Hetzner Provisioning/token            required
recovery-live       CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN                op://Personal/Keepling – Cloudflare DNS Cutover/token          required

# NOT YET LISTED, deliberately. The live host-replacement lane also needs
# KEEPLING_DNS_ZONE_ID, KEEPLING_DNS_RECORD_NAME, an SSH public key, the R2
# mirror credential and the backup cipher. No workflow consumes any of them
# today, because that lane is hardcoded NON_PASSING and never reads a
# credential. Uploading them now would put live credentials in a repository
# that has no code path able to use them. They go in with the lane wiring.
